# Pharmacy receipt → POS pack size (do not regress)

Cashier «В УП.» reads `product_attributes.units_in_pack`, not the receipt line.

## Invariants

1. On **post** (`PharmacyReceiptActivation`) and **posted mass/line sync** (`PharmacyReceiptPostedPriceSync`), copy line `unitsInPack` into product attribute `units_in_pack` via `PharmacyReceiptUnitsInPackSync` / `ProductAttributeService.upsertAttribute` (do not wipe other attributes).
2. When `unitsInPack > 1`, also set `soldIndividually=true`, `allowFraction=true`, and `quantityScale ≥ 3` so the cashier can sell by piece (do not leave a stale pack-only flag after sync).
3. Keep syncing cost / retail / VAT as today; pack size is additional, not instead of prices.
4. Dark POS cart price edit input must use `--pharm-cell-bg` / `--pharm-ink` (never hardcoded white bg + `color: inherit`).
5. Cashier `productSellByPiece`: honor explicit `sell_by_piece=false`; do **not** treat bare `soldIndividually=false` as pack-only when `units_in_pack > 1` (see `pharmacy-qty-modal.mdc`).

## Do not

- Assume changing only `stock_receipt_lines.units_in_pack` updates the cashier table.
- Call `saveAttributes` (full replace) just to set pack size.
- Sync pack size without enabling piece/fraction flags when units > 1.
